---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CurrentResearch from '../components/CurrentResearch.astro';
import profile from '../data/research-profile.json';
---
<BaseLayout title="Research" description="Human-centered AI research on imperfect feedback, preference learning, and evaluation reliability.">
  <div class="container-content py-14">
    <div class="max-w-[820px]">

      <span class="section-kicker mb-3">Research program · October 2026</span>
      <h1 class="mb-4">Learning from imperfect feedback</h1>
      <p class="lead mb-4">{profile.question}</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-10">{profile.profile} These collaborations, studies, and prototypes address different parts of the question. Together they motivate the next experiments; they do not establish a validated end-to-end adaptation system.</p>

      <!-- Research arc: how the projects connect (organizing frame, not a validated loop) -->
      <section id="arc" class="mb-12">
        <span class="section-kicker mb-2">Research arc</span>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-4">The projects connect as feedback measurement → state update and authorization → outcome evaluation. This is how the agenda is organized; it is not a claim that a complete learning loop has been validated.</p>
        <div class="space-y-0">
          <div class="arc-item"><span class="arc-index">01 · Understand the signal</span><p class="arc-question mt-1 mb-2">What does the feedback measure?</p><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] mb-3">Gaze, mouse behavior, and expressed preferences carry different kinds of evidence. I examine their collection and representation before treating them as learning signals.</p><a href="#collaborations" class="link-arrow">Current collaborations →</a></div>
          <div class="arc-item"><span class="arc-index">02 · Evaluate the decision</span><p class="arc-question mt-1 mb-2">What can a result establish?</p><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] mb-3">Memory-agent diagnostics and Evaluation Runtime separate observable failures, uncertain attribution, and evaluator judgments.</p><a href="/demo/eval-runtime/" class="link-arrow">Evaluation Runtime →</a></div>
          <div class="arc-item"><span class="arc-index">03 · Test adaptation</span><p class="arc-question mt-1 mb-2">Does using the signal help?</p><p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] mb-3">PMD tests known-user preference adaptation on held-out prompts. CheckMyCoach keeps human verification and information preservation in view. A reliable end-to-end learning loop remains a research goal.</p><a href="#projects" class="link-arrow">Studies and prototypes →</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <CurrentResearch />
      <p class="text-sm mb-12"><a href="/contributions/" class="link-arrow">Public, dated research and engineering contributions →</a></p>
      <!-- 3. Supporting work -->
      <section id="supporting" class="mb-12">
        <span class="section-kicker mb-2">Supporting work</span>
        <div class="related-list">
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Released · frozen methodological software</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">InteractionKit v1.0.0 is released and frozen. It implements typed specifications, composition constraints, derived schemas, and self-describing behavioral logs for AI interaction experiments. Its checks establish software contract conformance within the implemented scope; construct validity and cross-implementation equivalence have not been established.</span>
            <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/interactionkit/" class="link-arrow">InteractionKit →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Supporting evidence infrastructure</span>
            <span class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)]">Knowledge Compiler supports typed evidence objects, structural validation, partial provenance recovery, and quarantine of unresolved material. The current artifact exposes where evidence links remain incomplete; it does not establish source fidelity or validated downstream use.</span>
            <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/knowledge-compiler/" class="link-arrow">Knowledge Compiler →</a>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Historical context -->
      <section id="historical" class="mb-12">
        <span class="section-kicker mb-2">Historical context</span>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-5">
          Earlier work provides historical motivation rather than active research. M0 is a frozen measurement asset, not a validated instrument. MaxFitCalib-Bench is retained as engineering audit history, not a source of prevalence estimates or model rankings. CalTrust is frozen and simulation-only. The Precision Illusion behavioral thread is retired.
        </p>
        <div class="related-list">
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Retired behavioral thread</span>
            <a href="/blog/precision-illusion-intro/" class="link-arrow">Precision Illusion taxonomy →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Engineering audit · closed</span>
            <a href="/research/measuring-ai-reliability/fitcalib-bench/" class="link-arrow">MaxFitCalib-Bench audit →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="related-item">
            <span class="rel-role">Frozen · simulation only</span>
            <a href="/research/understanding-human-trust/caltrust/" class="link-arrow">CalTrust →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Current focus -->
      <section id="focus" class="mb-12">
        <div class="border-l-2 border-[var(--color-primary)] bg-[var(--color-primary-subtle)]/40 rounded-r-lg px-5 py-4">
          <p class="font-mono text-[0.62rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-primary)] uppercase tracking-wider mb-1">Current focus</p>
          <p class="font-sans text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed mb-2">
            I am working on feedback representation and evaluation reliability, and exploring controlled tests of adaptation. CheckMyCoach human validation remains in preparation; human evaluation has not yet been conducted.
          </p>
          <a href="/research/building-trustworthy-ai/checkmycoach/" class="link-arrow">CheckMyCoach project →</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 6. Reading the evidence -->
      <section id="evidence">
        <span class="section-kicker mb-2">Reading the evidence</span>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-dim)] leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          Software implementation, bounded machine evaluation, and human validation answer different questions. The first two are represented in these HCAI artifacts; completed human validation is not.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
